## 4. Integration Inventory

Before implementing or changing an integration, maintain an inventory.

| Integration | Purpose | Verification required |
|---|---|---|
| Frontend to backend | Retrieve and submit application data | API requests and responses work |
| Backend to database | Persist application data | Connection, queries, and migrations work |
| CSV/Excel import | Accept sales datasets | File validation and parsing work |
| Forecasting service | Generate sales predictions | Model execution and output validation work |
| AI provider | Generate explanations or recommendations | Provider configuration and error handling work |
| External business API | Retrieve approved external data | Authentication, limits, and schema are verified |
| File storage | Store uploaded datasets or reports | Access controls and lifecycle policies work |
| MCP service | Expose approved tools to compatible AI clients | Client/server connection and authorization work |
| Monitoring service | Collect operational metrics and errors | Events are received without leaking secrets |

Do not assume every integration is required. Select only those that support an approved product requirement.

