## 11. File Storage Integration

If uploaded datasets, exported reports, or generated artifacts need persistent storage, use an approved storage mechanism.

Possible options include local temporary storage, object storage, or a managed file-storage service. Choose based on deployment requirements.

### Requirements

- Enforce file access permissions.
- Use safe object names.
- Avoid public access by default.
- Validate file metadata.
- Set retention and deletion policies.
- Apply size limits.
- Protect sensitive business records.
- Avoid storing large files directly in the database unless the architecture requires it.

If the application runs on an ephemeral hosting filesystem, verify whether uploaded files survive restarts and redeployments. Do not rely on local persistent storage without confirming platform behavior.

