## 15. Integration Testing

Every integration should have automated or repeatable tests appropriate to its risk.

### Frontend and Backend

- [ ] Successful API request.
- [ ] Invalid input.
- [ ] Unauthorized request.
- [ ] Backend unavailable.
- [ ] Unexpected response format.
- [ ] Loading and error UI behavior.

### Database

- [ ] Valid connection.
- [ ] Query failure handling.
- [ ] Transaction behavior where required.
- [ ] Migration validation.
- [ ] Tenant isolation where applicable.

### File Import

- [ ] Valid CSV.
- [ ] Valid supported Excel file.
- [ ] Empty file.
- [ ] Missing required columns.
- [ ] Invalid numeric values.
- [ ] Unsupported file type.
- [ ] File exceeding configured limits.
- [ ] Unauthorized upload.

### Forecasting and AI

- [ ] Valid input data.
- [ ] Insufficient historical data.
- [ ] Invalid service output.
- [ ] Service timeout.
- [ ] Provider rate limit.
- [ ] Missing configuration.
- [ ] Unauthorized data access.
- [ ] No fabricated output after a failure.

### External APIs

- [ ] Successful response.
- [ ] Invalid credentials.
- [ ] Rate-limit response.
- [ ] Network timeout.
- [ ] Malformed response.
- [ ] Retry limit reached.

Use mocked external services for deterministic automated tests where appropriate. Run a smaller set of real integration tests in a controlled environment when credentials and service access are available.

